  "body": "The CL text dump, `Toolpath::is_prismatic` and `TiltedFrame::world_path` now keep a move's stated spindle C (`Move::rotary`, #33). Before, all three dropped or ignored it.\n\n### What was wrong (`main` 8b0d784)\n\n- `cl::text::to_text` wrote a C-live path without its C angle, and `from_text` had no word to read one. A C-live cut written through the headless binaries' dump (#279) read back as a 3-axis path cutting somewhere else.\n- `is_prismatic` looked only at the tool axis, so a C-live path counted as prismatic, and the dump wrote it as v1/v2.\n- `TiltedFrame::world_path` rebuilt every move with `rotary: None`.\n\n### What changed\n\n- `to_text` writes ` SC<millidegrees>` after any pose letters, the spelling the app's golden writer (`crates/app/tests/common`) already uses. `from_text` reads it back through `Move::with_rotary`. The reader matches the two-letter `SC` before the one-letter words, so it can't be taken for the arc sense `S`. A path with no C dumps byte for byte as before.\n- `is_prismatic` is false when any move states a C, so the dump (and the golden writer, which reads the same method) writes v4.\n- `world_path` copies `rotary` onto every move it maps, chords included. No tilted kind is C-stamped today (the rotary kinds take no tilt, `OpParams::tilt`), so this keeps the angle rather than refusing. Why, and what was dropped, is in `docs/decisions/295-cl-text-rotary.md`.\n- No golden holds an `SC` word, so none moved.\n\n### Tests (`crates/cl/src/cl/tests.rs`)\n\n- `a_stated_spindle_c_is_not_a_prismatic_path`\n- `the_text_dump_round_trips_a_stated_spindle_c`: v4 header; ` SC-90500` / ` SC-450250` on the moves; read back to -90.5 / -450.25 deg; nothing else moves; a path with no C has no `SC`.\n- `a_frame_keeps_a_stated_spindle_c_on_every_move_it_maps`: an upright frame and a 30-degree tilted one.\n- With `path.rs`, `text.rs` and `frame.rs` put back to `main` (`git stash` of those files only), all three fail: \"assertion failed: !c_live().is_prismatic()\", \"C None, want -90.5\", and \"a C-live path is not prismatic, so v4: ; HSMW-CL v1 ...\".\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local, built from upstream `main` 8b0d784 plus this commit)\n\n- The quick gate's plan for this diff, which for a `cl` change is every suite of every crate except the four slow binaries (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -DryRun`, run by hand with `-j 3` because other sessions had the CPU near 100%): 2472 pass, 29 ignored, 3 fail.\n- The 3 failures are the ui pixel snapshots (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`, `tool_editor_snapshot`), with the same pixel counts as clean `main` on this machine (1544, 1815, 2080). The owner's reviewer saw them pass on its own machine (#276's review).\n- `cargo clippy` over geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion, app and ui (`--all-targets -D warnings`): clean.\n- Not run: the slow release-tier binaries, Linux, macOS, and a C-live job through the headless binaries end to end.\n\nChangelog: The CL text dump keeps a C-axis live-tool path's spindle angle (the SC word), and such a path is no longer reported as prismatic (#295)\n\nFixes #295\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
